<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bảo Đại</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1913">1913</a>–<a href="/years/1997">1997</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Bao Dai, Nguyễn Phúc Vĩnh Thụy</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bảo Đại was the last emperor of the Nguyễn dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a>, reigning under French protection from 1926. He was made head of the Japanese-sponsored Empire of Vietnam in 1945 and abdicated to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viet-minh">Viet Minh</a> that August. The French returned him as head of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/state-of-vietnam">State of Vietnam</a> in 1949, but <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ngo-dinh-diem">Ngo Dinh Diem</a> deposed him in a referendum in 1955 and he died in exile in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bao-dai.jpg" alt="Bảo Đại" width="320" height="444" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Emperor_B%E1%BA%A3o_%C4%90%E1%BA%A1i_on_his_throne_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
